{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChK6UT8qwZAXjq7k981Y4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`HttpResponse(memoryview(b\"My Content\")).content` now returns `b'My Content'`, which is what the issue expects. The `responses` and `httpwrappers` test suites pass.\n\n**Cause:** a `memoryview` has `__iter__`, so the `content` setter treated it as an iterable of chunks and broke it up item by item. The single-value fallback also didn't recognise `memoryview`, so it got turned into its text form, `<memory at ...>`.\n\n**Fix:** two small changes in `django/http/response.py`:\n- **`content` setter (line 312):** `memoryview` is now handled like `bytes` and `str`, so it isn't iterated.\n- **`make_bytes` (line 232):** `memoryview` is converted with `bytes(value)`, the same way `bytes` is.\n\nI also checked that `response.write(memoryview(...))` works, since it goes through `make_bytes` too."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":734,"cache_read_input_tokens":19026,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":734},"output_tokens":302,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5b733569-7b83-4de2-8c61-23b05b77d8e2","uuid":"a0465cb3-374f-47a2-bbc4-214d13e8cfe7","timestamp":"2026-11-23T02:46:52.344Z","request_id":"req_011ChK6USmm9GyZtXo2piWhf"}
